# Navigation Structure

This app uses a fixed left sidebar for primary navigation on desktop (`md+`) and a fixed bottom tab bar on mobile. A fixed top navbar provides page context and actions on all breakpoints.

## Sidebar routes

Exactly **3** sidebar routes — do not add more without explicit user request:

| Route | Label | Icon |
|-------|-------|------|
| `/` | Home | `Home` |
| `/explore` | Explore | `Search` |
| `/profile` | Profile | `User` |

Source of truth: `config/navigation.ts` (`NAV_ITEMS`).

## Theme control

- Theme selection lives on the **Profile** page via `ThemeListBox` (`components/theme-list-box.tsx`).
- Use HeroUI `ListBox` with Light, Dark, and System options.
- **Never** put a theme switcher in the navbar.

## Mobile bottom tab bar

On viewports below `md`, primary navigation moves to `components/layout/mobile-tab-bar.tsx`:

- Reuses `NAV_ITEMS` from `config/navigation.ts`
- Fixed to the bottom with safe-area inset padding
- No top `border-separator` on the tab bar
- Avatar is hidden in the navbar on mobile (Profile is in the tab bar)

## Navbar layout

Standard navbar (`components/layout/navbar.tsx`):

- **Left:** Avatar (links to `/profile`, desktop only) + divider + current page title from `getPageTitle()`
- **Right:** Search icon button (links to `/explore`)

Do not add breadcrumbs, settings links, or extra nav items to the navbar unless explicitly requested.

## Adding new pages

If a new page is needed, prefer it as content within an existing route rather than adding a fourth sidebar item.
